// The translator's constants. Each is a program global read with
// (import name), which is not a call, so it may appear as a call argument.
//
// ch_dq, ch_sq, ch_nl: the byte codes of `"`, `'` and LF, the three the lexer
// names rather than spells.
//
// ch_eof: reading past the end of the source yields byte 0 (the NUL that
// mem_of_str copies, then the zeroed pad block lex_mem allocates behind it),
// so 0 is the lexer's end-of-input marker.
//
// tree_depth: how many directory levels a generated project's block tree has
// (emit/gen/out/path.id). 3^8 = 6561 leaf directories = 59049 functions. A path
// that runs out of room names two functions to one file, and the splitter
// then keeps only the last, so this is the one number to raise for a program
// with more block functions than that (cJSON, at 3000 lines, is about 3000).
//
// range_max: the most values a GNU range, `case a ... b:` or `[a ... b] = v`, may span; each becomes a
// case of its own.
//
// funcs_per_file: how many block functions share one generated file, which is
// id's own limit.
//
// rt_hidden: the runtime functions c_NAME that rt_names and libc_names do not list
// (the formatter and printk behind printf). A function the program defines under
// one of those names, or a rt_names or libc_names one, is emitted as u_NAME so the
// runtime's own c_NAME stays what the runtime's other code calls.
//
// bi_special: the builtins read by the parser, not called: constant_p is 0, choose_expr
// is the arm its constant condition picks and types_compatible_p compares two types
// (front/parse/code/ex/p/pf/post/call/bi/).
//
// sret_var: the name of the hidden first parameter of a function that returns a
// struct or union, a pointer to the caller's object the result is written to.
//
// op_names[i] is a binary operator token; op_levels[i] is its level, 0 being
// the loosest. Keep the two lists the same length and in the same order.
//
//   ||  0     &&  1     |  2     ^  3     &  4
//   ==  5  !=  5
//   <   6  >   6  <=  6  >=  6
//   <<  7  >>  7
//   +   8  -   8
//   *   9  /   9   %  9
//
// Note the C oddity this encodes: shift (7) is *looser* than additive (8), so
// `1 << 2 + 3` is `1 << (2 + 3)`.
//
// fl_ops[i] is an operator that has a floating-point operand and fl_fns[i] the
// crt function (crt/flt) that does it; keep the two lists the same length and in
// the same order. ld_fns[i] is the crt function (crt/ldbl) that does the
// arithmetic operator fl_ops[i] (the first four) on long doubles.
//
// esc_chars[i] means esc_vals[i]:
//
//   \a 7  \b 8  \t 9  \n 10  \v 11  \f 12  \r 13  \" 34  \' 39  \? 63  \\ 92
//
// spec_words: the counted specifier words, in the slot order sp uses.
//
// prim_names/prim_sizes/prim_signs: the eighteen canonical prim types every C
// combination collapses onto, their LP64 sizes (long and long long are both
// 8), and 1 where the type is signed. Plain `char` is signed on x86-64, which
// is the only place that matters. `void` is 1 byte, as GNU C makes sizeof(void)
// and arithmetic on a `void *`.
int ch_dq = 34;
int ch_sq = 39;
int ch_nl = 10;
int ch_eof = 0;
string sret_var = "__ret";
int tree_depth = 8;
int funcs_per_file = 3;
int range_max = 4096;
string[] op_names = ["||", "&&", "|", "^", "&", "==", "!=", "<", ">", "<=", ">=", "<<", ">>", "+", "-", "*", "/", "%"];
int[] op_levels = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 6, 6, 6, 6, 7, 7, 8, 8, 9, 9, 9];
