// The GCC atomic and __sync builtins. A call to atom_names[i] is rewritten
// (mid/pass/frame/atom) into a call of atom_fns[i] -- a function of rt/ext/builtin, or
// `memcpy` -- over the arguments atom_pick[i] names (digits, the order in which
// they are passed on), then the constant atom_ops[i] when it is not -1, then the
// size of the object the first argument points at when atom_how[i] is odd; when
// atom_how[i] is 2 or more the value is cast to the type of that object. An entry
// whose function is "" is a constant, the value atom_ops[i]: a fence is 0 and a
// lock-free test is 1. atom_arity[i] is how many arguments the call needs at
// least; the order arguments are not passed on, because the program has one thread.
// Operation codes: 0 exchange, 1 add, 2 sub, 3 and, 4 or, 5 xor, 6 nand, and 8 more
// when the new value is what the call answers.
